580
00:19:20,499 --> 00:19:21,474
Pattern three.

581
00:19:21,654 --> 00:19:22,629
Weak competition.

582
00:19:22,809 --> 00:19:24,951
When fewer people are willing to do

583
00:19:24,951 --> 00:19:26,726
the work, the ones who do can

584
00:19:26,726 --> 00:19:29,358
often charge fair prices and keep customers

585
00:19:29,358 --> 00:19:29,787
longer.

586
00:19:29,967 --> 00:19:32,336
That doesn't mean there's no competition,

587
00:19:32,336 --> 00:19:34,762
but the competition is usually smaller and

588
00:19:34,762 --> 00:19:37,246
less aggressive than in popular industries.

589
00:19:37,596 --> 00:19:38,513
Pattern four.

590
00:19:38,693 --> 00:19:40,144
Reusable assets.

591
00:19:40,324 --> 00:19:42,696
A dumpster, a portable toilet,

592
00:19:42,696 --> 00:19:43,882
a storage unit,

593
00:19:43,882 --> 00:19:44,910
a pump truck.

594
00:19:45,090 --> 00:19:47,665
Each one gets used again and again

595
00:19:47,665 --> 00:19:48,422
for years.

596
00:19:48,602 --> 00:19:51,058
Every additional rental or job on the

597
00:19:51,058 --> 00:19:53,912
same asset spreads the purchase cost wider,

598
00:19:53,912 --> 00:19:56,235
which is how margins improve as you

599
00:19:56,235 --> 00:19:56,567
grow.

600
00:19:56,917 --> 00:19:58,066
An illustration.

601
00:19:58,246 --> 00:20:00,969
A dumpster bought for six thousand dollars,

602
00:20:00,969 --> 00:20:03,376
rented twice a month at a contribution

603
00:20:03,376 --> 00:20:05,972
of two hundred dollars after disposal and

604
00:20:05,972 --> 00:20:08,822
fuel, earns about four thousand eight hundred

605
00:20:08,822 --> 00:20:10,785
dollars a year before overhead.

606
00:20:11,135 --> 00:20:12,783
Here's a simple illustration.

607
00:20:12,963 --> 00:20:16,005
Say a dumpster costs six thousand dollars.

608
00:20:16,185 --> 00:20:18,735
Say it's rented about twice a month,

609
00:20:18,735 --> 00:20:20,434
and after disposal fees,

610
00:20:20,434 --> 00:20:21,922
fuel and driver time,

611
00:20:21,922 --> 00:20:24,684
each rental leaves two hundred dollars.

612
00:20:24,864 --> 00:20:27,833
That's about four thousand eight hundred dollars

613
00:20:27,833 --> 00:20:29,070
a year from one box,

614
00:20:29,070 --> 00:20:30,988
before overhead like insurance,

615
00:20:30,988 --> 00:20:33,153
office costs and the truck payment.

616
00:20:33,333 --> 00:20:35,218
The box could pay for itself in

617
00:20:35,218 --> 00:20:36,981
a little over a year and keep

618
00:20:36,981 --> 00:20:38,743
working for many years after.

619
00:20:39,094 --> 00:20:40,663
But notice the assumption:

620
00:20:40,663 --> 00:20:41,509
twice a month.

621
00:20:41,689 --> 00:20:44,100
If that dumpster sits idle half the

622
00:20:44,100 --> 00:20:45,961
time, the math falls apart.

623
00:20:46,141 --> 00:20:48,560
That's the big lesson of asset based

624
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:49,299
businesses.

625
00:20:49,479 --> 00:20:51,592
Owning the equipment isn't the hard part.

626
00:20:51,772 --> 00:20:53,316
Keeping it busy is.

627
00:20:53,496 --> 00:20:56,004
Utilization, meaning the share of time your

628
00:20:56,004 --> 00:20:57,113
assets are earning,

629
00:20:57,113 --> 00:20:59,446
is the number that decides whether these

630
00:20:59,446 --> 00:21:00,729
businesses make money.

631
00:21:01,079 --> 00:21:03,418
Labor businesses, like junk removal,

632
00:21:03,418 --> 00:21:06,081
commercial cleaning and pressure washing,

633
00:21:06,081 --> 00:21:07,511
have a different math.

634
00:21:07,691 --> 00:21:09,233
They need less equipment,

635
00:21:09,233 --> 00:21:11,084
but profit depends on pricing,

636
00:21:11,084 --> 00:21:13,182
crew efficiency and route density.

637
00:21:13,362 --> 00:21:15,519
A crew that finishes four jobs a

638
00:21:15,519 --> 00:21:18,080
day close together earns far more than

639
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:20,372
a crew that drives across town for

640
00:21:20,372 --> 00:21:20,642
two.

641
00:21:20,992 --> 00:21:23,015
Let's make this real with three made

642
00:21:23,015 --> 00:21:24,363
up but realistic owners,

643
00:21:24,363 --> 00:21:26,611
each starting a different ugly business.

644
00:21:26,961 --> 00:21:29,649
Owner one starts a junk removal company

645
00:21:29,649 --> 00:21:31,510
with a used box truck and a

646
00:21:31,510 --> 00:21:33,509
friend as his first employee.

647
00:21:33,689 --> 00:21:35,082
The first year is hard.

648
00:21:35,262 --> 00:21:37,659
He learns that he underpriced big jobs,

649
00:21:37,659 --> 00:21:39,994
that dump fees eat more than expected,

650
00:21:39,994 --> 00:21:41,961
and that reviews are everything.

651
00:21:42,141 --> 00:21:42,942
In year two,

652
00:21:42,942 --> 00:21:44,078
he raises prices,

653
00:21:44,078 --> 00:21:47,485
builds relationships with three real estate offices

654
00:21:47,485 --> 00:21:49,222
and two property managers,

655
00:21:49,222 --> 00:21:51,626
and starts getting steady referrals.

656
00:21:51,806 --> 00:21:52,738
By year three,

657
00:21:52,738 --> 00:21:54,936
he runs two crews and spends most

658
00:21:54,936 --> 00:21:57,333
of his time on sales and scheduling.

659
00:21:57,683 --> 00:22:00,529
Owner two buys an existing pest control

660
00:22:00,529 --> 00:22:02,718
company from a retiring owner,

661
00:22:02,718 --> 00:22:05,126
using an SBA loan and some seller

662
00:22:05,126 --> 00:22:05,856
financing.

663
00:22:06,036 --> 00:22:09,346
She inherits several hundred customers on service

664
00:22:09,346 --> 00:22:09,751
plans.

665
00:22:09,931 --> 00:22:12,175
Her first year is about not losing

666
00:22:12,175 --> 00:22:14,353
anyone: she calls every customer,

667
00:22:14,353 --> 00:22:16,068
keeps the old technicians,

668
00:22:16,068 --> 00:22:17,652
and improves scheduling.

669
00:22:17,832 --> 00:22:20,068
Her second year is about growth:

670
00:22:20,068 --> 00:22:23,072
she adds commercial contracts and a termite

671
00:22:23,072 --> 00:22:25,448
inspection service for home sales.

672
00:22:25,798 --> 00:22:28,602
Owner three starts a pressure washing business

673
00:22:28,602 --> 00:22:30,674
on weekends while keeping his job.

674
00:22:30,854 --> 00:22:32,749
He buys modest equipment,

675
00:22:32,749 --> 00:22:35,023
posts before and after photos,

676
00:22:35,023 --> 00:22:37,297
and books driveways and decks.

677
00:22:37,477 --> 00:22:38,529
After a season,

678
00:22:38,529 --> 00:22:41,612
he notices that restaurants and gas stations

679
00:22:41,612 --> 00:22:43,364
pay for regular cleaning.

680
00:22:43,544 --> 00:22:45,830
He pitches a dozen local businesses,

681
00:22:45,830 --> 00:22:47,671
lands four monthly contracts,

682
00:22:47,671 --> 00:22:50,211
and that recurring revenue gives him the

683
00:22:50,211 --> 00:22:52,434
confidence to go full time the next

684
00:22:52,434 --> 00:22:52,878
spring.

685
00:22:53,228 --> 00:22:54,588
Three different paths,

686
00:22:54,588 --> 00:22:55,886
but the same lessons.

687
00:22:56,066 --> 00:22:57,230
Price for profit,

688
00:22:57,230 --> 00:22:58,667
not just to win jobs.

689
00:22:58,847 --> 00:23:00,380
Chase recurring revenue.

690
00:23:00,560 --> 00:23:03,180
Build relationships with people who send you

691
00:23:03,180 --> 00:23:03,776
customers.

692
00:23:03,956 --> 00:23:06,450
And keep risk small until the business

693
00:23:06,450 --> 00:23:07,369
proves itself.

694
00:23:07,549 --> 00:23:09,354
None of them got rich overnight,

695
00:23:09,354 --> 00:23:11,497
but each one built something that pays

696
00:23:11,497 --> 00:23:13,359
far more than the work looks like

697
00:23:13,359 --> 00:23:13,923
it should.

698
00:23:14,273 --> 00:23:16,516
Ugly businesses can make good money,

699
00:23:16,516 --> 00:23:18,011
but plenty of them fail.

700
00:23:18,191 --> 00:23:20,339
Here are eight mistakes that sink them.

701
00:23:20,689 --> 00:23:21,606
Mistake one.

702
00:23:21,786 --> 00:23:22,599
Underpricing.

703
00:23:22,779 --> 00:23:25,544
New owners often charge too little to

704
00:23:25,544 --> 00:23:28,533
win jobs, then discover they can't cover

705
00:23:28,533 --> 00:23:30,028
fuel, disposal fees,

706
00:23:30,028 --> 00:23:31,672
insurance and repairs.

707
00:23:31,852 --> 00:23:34,180
Know your full cost per job before

708
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:35,207
you set prices.

709
00:23:35,387 --> 00:23:36,537
Mistake two.

710
00:23:36,717 --> 00:23:38,133
Skipping the paperwork.

711
00:23:38,313 --> 00:23:40,913
Operating without the right licenses,

712
00:23:40,913 --> 00:23:43,513
permits or insurance can bring fines,

713
00:23:43,513 --> 00:23:46,183
lawsuits, or a shutdown that wipes out

714
00:23:46,183 --> 00:23:47,659
everything you built.

715
00:23:48,009 --> 00:23:49,100
Mistake three.

716
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:51,811
Buying too much equipment too soon.

717
00:23:51,991 --> 00:23:53,823
A shiny new truck with a big

718
00:23:53,823 --> 00:23:56,245
loan payment can sink a business that

719
00:23:56,245 --> 00:23:58,469
hasn't found enough customers yet.

720
00:23:58,649 --> 00:23:59,729
Mistake four.

721
00:23:59,909 --> 00:24:01,314
Ignoring utilization.

722
00:24:01,494 --> 00:24:04,835
Idle dumpsters, empty storage units and parked

723
00:24:04,835 --> 00:24:07,450
trucks still cost money every month.

724
00:24:07,630 --> 00:24:09,315
Track how busy your assets are,

725
00:24:09,315 --> 00:24:11,109
and don't buy more until the ones

726
00:24:11,109 --> 00:24:12,251
you have are working.

727
00:24:12,601 --> 00:24:13,541
Mistake five.

728
00:24:13,721 --> 00:24:14,801
Poor communication.

729
00:24:14,981 --> 00:24:16,375
In service businesses,

730
00:24:16,375 --> 00:24:18,656
showing up on time and answering the

731
00:24:18,656 --> 00:24:21,761
phone wins more customers than any advertisement.

732
00:24:21,941 --> 00:24:23,717
Missed calls are missed money.

733
00:24:23,897 --> 00:24:25,175
Mistake six.

734
00:24:25,355 --> 00:24:26,794
Neglecting reviews.

735
00:24:26,974 --> 00:24:28,364
In local businesses,

736
00:24:28,364 --> 00:24:31,143
online reviews often decide who gets the

737
00:24:31,143 --> 00:24:31,490
call.

738
00:24:31,670 --> 00:24:34,673
Ask happy customers for reviews and respond

739
00:24:34,673 --> 00:24:36,698
politely to the unhappy ones.

740
00:24:37,048 --> 00:24:38,058
Mistake seven.

741
00:24:38,238 --> 00:24:40,467
Doing everything yourself forever.

742
00:24:40,647 --> 00:24:43,083
Owners who never hire or train anyone

743
00:24:43,083 --> 00:24:44,861
hit a ceiling and burn out.

744
00:24:45,041 --> 00:24:46,605
Build simple systems early,

745
00:24:46,605 --> 00:24:48,399
so someone else can do the work

746
00:24:48,399 --> 00:24:49,442
the way you would.

747
00:24:49,622 --> 00:24:50,841
And mistake eight.

748
00:24:51,021 --> 00:24:53,401
Mixing personal and business money.

749
00:24:53,581 --> 00:24:55,141
Separate bank accounts,

750
00:24:55,141 --> 00:24:57,651
clean records and money set aside for

751
00:24:57,651 --> 00:25:00,296
taxes keep a good business from turning

752
00:25:00,296 --> 00:25:01,789
into a financial mess.

753
00:25:02,139 --> 00:25:04,588
Let's sort these fifteen businesses by how

754
00:25:04,588 --> 00:25:06,572
much money it roughly takes to get

755
00:25:06,572 --> 00:25:07,038
started.

756
00:25:07,218 --> 00:25:08,802
These are broad tiers,

757
00:25:08,802 --> 00:25:11,394
not quotes, and real costs depend on

758
00:25:11,394 --> 00:25:13,771
your area and whether you buy new

759
00:25:13,771 --> 00:25:14,347
or used.

760
00:25:14,697 --> 00:25:17,146
Tier one, lower startup costs.

761
00:25:17,326 --> 00:25:19,142
Junk removal with a trailer,

762
00:25:19,142 --> 00:25:21,606
pressure washing, commercial cleaning,

763
00:25:21,606 --> 00:25:24,525
and trash can cleaning with modest equipment.

764
00:25:24,705 --> 00:25:27,124
Many people start these for thousands to

765
00:25:27,124 --> 00:25:28,879
tens of thousands of dollars,

766
00:25:28,879 --> 00:25:30,452
often while keeping a job.

767
00:25:30,632 --> 00:25:32,706
The tradeoff is more competition,

768
00:25:32,706 --> 00:25:35,032
because the door is open to everyone.

769
00:25:35,382 --> 00:25:38,029
Tier two, moderate startup costs.

770
00:25:38,209 --> 00:25:40,890
Pest control, dead animal removal,

771
00:25:40,890 --> 00:25:43,886
drain cleaning, and biohazard cleanup.

772
00:25:44,066 --> 00:25:45,419
These need training,

773
00:25:45,419 --> 00:25:48,532
licenses, insurance and specialized equipment,

774
00:25:48,532 --> 00:25:50,765
but not necessarily heavy trucks.

775
00:25:50,945 --> 00:25:54,009
The licensing and training requirements also keep

776
00:25:54,009 --> 00:25:55,322
some competitors out.

777
00:25:55,672 --> 00:25:58,319
Tier three, higher startup costs.

778
00:25:58,499 --> 00:26:01,415
Septic pumping, grease trap cleaning,

779
00:26:01,415 --> 00:26:05,278
dumpster rental and portable toilets need trucks,

780
00:26:05,278 --> 00:26:06,854
containers or units,

781
00:26:06,854 --> 00:26:08,983
plus disposal arrangements.

782
00:26:09,163 --> 00:26:10,216
And tier four,

783
00:26:10,216 --> 00:26:11,496
the most capital:

784
00:26:11,496 --> 00:26:14,582
self storage, mobile home parks and scrap

785
00:26:14,582 --> 00:26:17,443
yards, which are closer to real estate

786
00:26:17,443 --> 00:26:18,195
investing.

787
00:26:18,375 --> 00:26:22,038
Higher capital requirements usually mean fewer competitors,

788
00:26:22,038 --> 00:26:24,087
but more risk if things go wrong.

789
00:26:24,437 --> 00:26:25,493
Second angle.

790
00:26:25,673 --> 00:26:26,718
The psychology.

791
00:26:26,898 --> 00:26:28,859
Why do so many people avoid these

792
00:26:28,859 --> 00:26:31,236
businesses, and why is that an advantage

793
00:26:31,236 --> 00:26:32,425
for those who don't?

794
00:26:32,775 --> 00:26:34,818
The first reason is status.

795
00:26:34,998 --> 00:26:37,000
Many people care what others think of

796
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:37,541
their job.

797
00:26:37,721 --> 00:26:39,739
Saying you own a tech startup sounds

798
00:26:39,739 --> 00:26:40,356
impressive.

799
00:26:40,536 --> 00:26:42,603
Saying you own a septic company gets

800
00:26:42,603 --> 00:26:43,694
a laugh at a party.

801
00:26:43,874 --> 00:26:45,793
But the bank doesn't care how your

802
00:26:45,793 --> 00:26:46,695
business sounds.

803
00:26:46,875 --> 00:26:48,640
It cares about cash flow.

804
00:26:48,820 --> 00:26:50,794
Willing to give up status can mean

805
00:26:50,794 --> 00:26:51,606
gaining money.

806
00:26:51,957 --> 00:26:53,989
The second reason is disgust.

807
00:26:54,169 --> 00:26:56,678
Our brains are wired to avoid dirt,

808
00:26:56,678 --> 00:26:57,826
waste and decay.

809
00:26:58,006 --> 00:27:00,661
That instinct kept our ancestors alive,

810
00:27:00,661 --> 00:27:02,840
but it also creates a barrier to

811
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:04,542
entry in modern business.

812
00:27:04,722 --> 00:27:06,983
Every person who says that's gross is

813
00:27:06,983 --> 00:27:08,205
one less competitor.

814
00:27:08,385 --> 00:27:10,411
The disgust barrier is a moat that

815
00:27:10,411 --> 00:27:11,961
protects these businesses.

816
00:27:12,311 --> 00:27:14,563
The third reason is the passion trap.

817
00:27:14,743 --> 00:27:17,151
People are told to follow their passion,

818
00:27:17,151 --> 00:27:19,859
so they open businesses in crowded industries

819
00:27:19,859 --> 00:27:22,207
they love, like restaurants or fashion,

820
00:27:22,207 --> 00:27:23,892
where competition is fierce.

821
00:27:24,072 --> 00:27:27,085
Many successful ugly business owners say the

822
00:27:27,085 --> 00:27:28,386
passion came later,

823
00:27:28,386 --> 00:27:30,783
from building something that works,

824
00:27:30,783 --> 00:27:33,865
serving customers well and seeing the profits

825
00:27:33,865 --> 00:27:34,207
grow.

826
00:27:34,557 --> 00:27:36,821
The fourth reason is invisibility.

827
00:27:37,001 --> 00:27:40,230
Nobody posts their septic company on social

828
00:27:40,230 --> 00:27:40,681
media.

829
00:27:40,861 --> 00:27:42,974
You don't see these businesses in movies.

830
00:27:43,154 --> 00:27:45,871
So young people rarely even consider them.

831
00:27:46,051 --> 00:27:48,793
Meanwhile, many owners of these companies are

832
00:27:48,793 --> 00:27:52,266
approaching retirement, which may create opportunities to

833
00:27:52,266 --> 00:27:55,130
buy established businesses in the coming years.

834
00:27:55,480 --> 00:27:56,385
Here's the takeaway.

835
00:27:56,565 --> 00:27:58,526
The feeling of not wanting to do

836
00:27:58,526 --> 00:27:59,384
a job is real,

837
00:27:59,384 --> 00:28:00,977
but it's also information.

838
00:28:01,157 --> 00:28:03,303
It tells you most other people feel

839
00:28:03,303 --> 00:28:04,100
the same way,

840
00:28:04,100 --> 00:28:06,062
which is exactly why the job can

841
00:28:06,062 --> 00:28:06,614
pay well.

842
00:28:06,964 --> 00:28:07,811
Third angle.

843
00:28:07,991 --> 00:28:08,769
The playbook.

844
00:28:08,949 --> 00:28:10,487
How do you choose one of these

845
00:28:10,487 --> 00:28:13,256
businesses and get started without risking everything?

846
00:28:13,607 --> 00:28:14,385
Step one.

847
00:28:14,565 --> 00:28:16,538
Be honest about what you can tolerate.

848
00:28:16,718 --> 00:28:19,106
Smell, blood, heavy lifting,

849
00:28:19,106 --> 00:28:21,153
night work, emergencies.

850
00:28:21,333 --> 00:28:23,841
Each business has its own version of

851
00:28:23,841 --> 00:28:24,189
ugly.

852
00:28:24,369 --> 00:28:25,706
Pick the one you can do for

853
00:28:25,706 --> 00:28:26,993
years without burning out.

854
00:28:27,173 --> 00:28:28,137
Step two.

855
00:28:28,317 --> 00:28:29,873
Study your local market.

856
00:28:30,053 --> 00:28:32,381
Search for providers in your area,

857
00:28:32,381 --> 00:28:33,682
read their reviews,

858
00:28:33,682 --> 00:28:34,915
and look for gaps,

859
00:28:34,915 --> 00:28:36,627
like slow response times,

860
00:28:36,627 --> 00:28:39,229
bad service or no one covering certain

861
00:28:39,229 --> 00:28:40,188
neighborhoods.

862
00:28:40,538 --> 00:28:41,443
Step three.

863
00:28:41,623 --> 00:28:42,726
Learn the rules.

864
00:28:42,906 --> 00:28:45,057
Licenses, permits, insurance,

865
00:28:45,057 --> 00:28:48,690
disposal requirements and safety training vary by

866
00:28:48,690 --> 00:28:49,803
state and city.

867
00:28:49,983 --> 00:28:52,652
Call your local licensing office and talk

868
00:28:52,652 --> 00:28:55,452
to an insurance agent before spending money

869
00:28:55,452 --> 00:28:56,298
on equipment.

870
00:28:56,478 --> 00:28:57,349
Step four.

871
00:28:57,529 --> 00:28:59,528
Work in the industry first if you

872
00:28:59,528 --> 00:28:59,770
can.

873
00:28:59,950 --> 00:29:02,243
A few months on someone else's crew

874
00:29:02,243 --> 00:29:03,554
teaches you pricing,

875
00:29:03,554 --> 00:29:06,568
problems and customers faster than any course.

876
00:29:06,918 --> 00:29:07,881
Step five.

877
00:29:08,061 --> 00:29:09,071
Start small.

878
00:29:09,251 --> 00:29:11,921
Many of these businesses can start with

879
00:29:11,921 --> 00:29:13,495
one truck, one trailer,

880
00:29:13,495 --> 00:29:15,823
a few containers or a single crew.

881
00:29:16,003 --> 00:29:18,267
Test demand before borrowing big.

882
00:29:18,447 --> 00:29:19,689
Step six.

883
00:29:19,869 --> 00:29:21,413
Chase recurring revenue.

884
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:25,328
Service plans, contracts and subscriptions turn one

885
00:29:25,328 --> 00:29:28,184
time customers into predictable income,

886
00:29:28,184 --> 00:29:31,113
which is what makes a business valuable.

887
00:29:31,463 --> 00:29:32,450
Step seven.

888
00:29:32,630 --> 00:29:34,743
Consider buying instead of starting.

889
00:29:34,923 --> 00:29:38,110
Many established businesses in these industries are

890
00:29:38,110 --> 00:29:40,298
owned by people nearing retirement.

891
00:29:40,478 --> 00:29:42,674
Buying one can give you customers,

892
00:29:42,674 --> 00:29:45,064
equipment and cash flow from day one.

893
00:29:45,244 --> 00:29:48,344
The Small Business Administration has loan programs

894
00:29:48,344 --> 00:29:50,472
that can be used to buy businesses,

895
00:29:50,472 --> 00:29:53,329
though they come with requirements and personal

896
00:29:53,329 --> 00:29:53,998
guarantees.

897
00:29:54,348 --> 00:29:55,335
And step eight.

898
00:29:55,515 --> 00:29:57,198
Keep your foundation solid.

899
00:29:57,378 --> 00:29:58,805
Keep an emergency fund,

900
00:29:58,805 --> 00:30:00,977
don't put all your savings into one

901
00:30:00,977 --> 00:30:03,769
truck, and keep investing for retirement even

902
00:30:03,769 --> 00:30:04,762
while you build.

903
00:30:04,942 --> 00:30:07,506
A business is a powerful wealth builder,

904
00:30:07,506 --> 00:30:10,006
but your safety net should never depend

905
00:30:10,006 --> 00:30:10,968
entirely on it.

906
00:30:11,318 --> 00:30:13,463
Before you commit to any of these,

907
00:30:13,463 --> 00:30:15,797
run it through a simple five question

908
00:30:15,797 --> 00:30:16,113
test.

909
00:30:16,293 --> 00:30:18,013
If the answer to most of them

910
00:30:18,013 --> 00:30:19,673
is yes, you may have found a

911
00:30:19,673 --> 00:30:20,681
good opportunity.

912
00:30:21,031 --> 00:30:21,867
Question one.

913
00:30:22,047 --> 00:30:23,575
Is the service required,

914
00:30:23,575 --> 00:30:24,404
not optional?

915
00:30:24,584 --> 00:30:25,501
Question two.

916
00:30:25,681 --> 00:30:27,575
Will customers need it again,

917
00:30:27,575 --> 00:30:29,013
ideally on a schedule?

918
00:30:29,193 --> 00:30:30,214
Question three.

919
00:30:30,394 --> 00:30:32,318
Are there few good providers in my

920
00:30:32,318 --> 00:30:34,806
area, judging by search results and reviews?

921
00:30:34,986 --> 00:30:35,961
Question four.

922
00:30:36,141 --> 00:30:37,987
Can I start small and test it

923
00:30:37,987 --> 00:30:39,323
before borrowing big?

924
00:30:39,503 --> 00:30:40,757
And question five.

925
00:30:40,937 --> 00:30:43,277
Can I picture myself doing or managing

926
00:30:43,277 --> 00:30:45,372
this work for at least five years?

927
00:30:45,722 --> 00:30:48,499
Septic pumping scores high on required and

928
00:30:48,499 --> 00:30:49,623
recurring demand.

929
00:30:49,803 --> 00:30:52,717
Junk removal scores high on starting small.

930
00:30:52,897 --> 00:30:55,293
Self storage scores high on low labor

931
00:30:55,293 --> 00:30:57,495
but fails the start small test for

932
00:30:57,495 --> 00:30:58,272
most people.

933
00:30:58,452 --> 00:31:00,164
There's no perfect business,

934
00:31:00,164 --> 00:31:02,182
only the best fit for your money,

935
00:31:02,182 --> 00:31:04,873
your skills, your location and your stomach.

936
00:31:05,053 --> 00:31:07,446
Score two or three options honestly,

937
00:31:07,446 --> 00:31:09,906
and the right one usually stands out.

938
00:31:10,256 --> 00:31:12,464
And remember, the goal isn't to own

939
00:31:12,464 --> 00:31:14,041
an ugly business forever.

940
00:31:14,221 --> 00:31:16,008
Many owners build the company,

941
00:31:16,008 --> 00:31:16,902
hire a manager,

942
00:31:16,902 --> 00:31:18,273
and eventually sell it.

943
00:31:18,453 --> 00:31:20,608
A business with recurring revenue,

944
00:31:20,608 --> 00:31:22,637
clean books and a team that runs

945
00:31:22,637 --> 00:31:25,046
without the owner can sell for several

946
00:31:25,046 --> 00:31:26,568
times its yearly profit.

947
00:31:26,748 --> 00:31:28,481
That sale can be the moment the

948
00:31:28,481 --> 00:31:30,382
dirty work turns into real wealth.

949
00:31:30,732 --> 00:31:32,951
Let me answer a few common questions

950
00:31:32,951 --> 00:31:34,308
about ugly businesses.

951
00:31:34,658 --> 00:31:35,540
Question one.

952
00:31:35,720 --> 00:31:38,007
Which one is the easiest to start?

953
00:31:38,187 --> 00:31:40,806
Businesses with low equipment costs,

954
00:31:40,806 --> 00:31:42,115
like junk removal,

955
00:31:42,115 --> 00:31:45,097
pressure washing and commercial cleaning,

956
00:31:45,097 --> 00:31:46,988
are often easier to start.

957
00:31:47,168 --> 00:31:49,358
But easy to start also means easy

958
00:31:49,358 --> 00:31:51,017
for competitors to start,

959
00:31:51,017 --> 00:31:53,472
so service quality becomes your edge.

960
00:31:53,652 --> 00:31:54,558
Question two.

961
00:31:54,738 --> 00:31:56,340
Which ones need the most money?

962
00:31:56,520 --> 00:31:58,755
Self storage, mobile home parks,

963
00:31:58,755 --> 00:32:01,759
scrap yards and truck based businesses like

964
00:32:01,759 --> 00:32:04,902
septic pumping usually need the most capital.

965
00:32:05,252 --> 00:32:06,366
Question three.

966
00:32:06,546 --> 00:32:08,192
Can I run one without doing the

967
00:32:08,192 --> 00:32:09,147
dirty work myself?

968
00:32:09,327 --> 00:32:12,590
Eventually, many owners hire crews and focus

969
00:32:12,590 --> 00:32:15,260
on sales, scheduling and management.

970
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:17,844
But most successful owners did the work

971
00:32:17,844 --> 00:32:18,891
at the beginning,

972
00:32:18,891 --> 00:32:21,110
which taught them how to price jobs,

973
00:32:21,110 --> 00:32:23,021
train people and spot problems.

974
00:32:23,201 --> 00:32:24,118
Question four.

975
00:32:24,298 --> 00:32:26,307
Are these businesses recession proof?

976
00:32:26,487 --> 00:32:28,566
Nothing is fully recession proof,

977
00:32:28,566 --> 00:32:30,897
but required services tend to hold up

978
00:32:30,897 --> 00:32:32,536
better than optional ones.

979
00:32:32,886 --> 00:32:33,896
Question five.

980
00:32:34,076 --> 00:32:35,841
How do I find customers?

981
00:32:36,021 --> 00:32:37,497
Local search listings,

982
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:41,122
online reviews, relationships with real estate agents,

983
00:32:41,122 --> 00:32:44,679
property managers, contractors and restaurant owners,

984
00:32:44,679 --> 00:32:47,431
and simply being the company that answers

985
00:32:47,431 --> 00:32:49,511
the phone and shows up on time.

986
00:32:49,691 --> 00:32:51,683
In many of these industries,

987
00:32:51,683 --> 00:32:54,813
being reliable is a competitive advantage by

988
00:32:54,813 --> 00:32:55,311
itself.

989
00:32:55,661 --> 00:32:56,799
Question six.

990
00:32:56,979 --> 00:32:58,500
Do I need a college degree?

991
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:00,773
For most of these businesses,

992
00:33:00,773 --> 00:33:00,990
no.

993
00:33:01,170 --> 00:33:02,863
What you need is training,

994
00:33:02,863 --> 00:33:04,492
licensing where required,

995
00:33:04,492 --> 00:33:07,422
business skills like pricing and bookkeeping,

996
00:33:07,422 --> 00:33:09,181
and a willingness to learn.

997
00:33:09,361 --> 00:33:11,741
Many owners take short courses,

998
00:33:11,741 --> 00:33:14,504
certifications, or learn on the job.

999
00:33:14,684 --> 00:33:15,671
Question seven.

1000
00:33:15,851 --> 00:33:17,244
What about taxes?

1001
00:33:17,424 --> 00:33:20,314
Business owners pay income tax plus self

1002
00:33:20,314 --> 00:33:22,192
employment tax on profits,

1003
00:33:22,192 --> 00:33:25,226
and often need to make quarterly estimated

1004
00:33:25,226 --> 00:33:25,876
payments.

1005
00:33:26,056 --> 00:33:28,959
A good accountant usually pays for themselves.

1006
00:33:29,309 --> 00:33:30,168
Question eight.

1007
00:33:30,348 --> 00:33:31,927
What if I start and hate it?

1008
00:33:32,107 --> 00:33:33,848
That's why starting small matters.

1009
00:33:34,028 --> 00:33:36,205
If you test the business on weekends

1010
00:33:36,205 --> 00:33:38,079
or work for someone else first,

1011
00:33:38,079 --> 00:33:40,074
the cost of changing your mind is

1012
00:33:40,074 --> 00:33:40,437
small.

1013
00:33:40,617 --> 00:33:42,544
Used equipment can often be sold.

1014
00:33:42,724 --> 00:33:45,114
The bigger danger is borrowing heavily before

1015
00:33:45,114 --> 00:33:46,920
you know whether you can stand the

1016
00:33:46,920 --> 00:33:47,717
work for years.

1017
00:33:48,067 --> 00:33:48,926
Question nine.

1018
00:33:49,106 --> 00:33:51,144
Is it better to pick one business

1019
00:33:51,144 --> 00:33:52,194
or combine a few?

1020
00:33:52,374 --> 00:33:55,158
Many owners combine related services,

1021
00:33:55,158 --> 00:33:58,394
like pest control with dead animal removal,

1022
00:33:58,394 --> 00:34:01,479
or junk removal with light demolition and

1023
00:34:01,479 --> 00:34:02,231
cleanouts.

1024
00:34:02,411 --> 00:34:04,989
Combining services lets you sell more to

1025
00:34:04,989 --> 00:34:07,439
the same customer using the same truck

1026
00:34:07,439 --> 00:34:08,019
and crew.

1027
00:34:08,199 --> 00:34:10,319
But start with one service and master

1028
00:34:10,319 --> 00:34:11,809
it before you add another.

1029
00:34:12,160 --> 00:34:12,984
Question ten.

1030
00:34:13,164 --> 00:34:14,804
How do I know if a business

1031
00:34:14,804 --> 00:34:15,776
is worth buying?

1032
00:34:15,956 --> 00:34:17,910
Look at at least three years of

1033
00:34:17,910 --> 00:34:20,998
tax returns, the percentage of recurring revenue,

1034
00:34:20,998 --> 00:34:22,573
the age of the equipment,

1035
00:34:22,573 --> 00:34:24,842
how dependent the business is on the

1036
00:34:24,842 --> 00:34:26,858
owner, and the customer reviews.

1037
00:34:27,038 --> 00:34:28,965
Then have an accountant and a lawyer

1038
00:34:28,965 --> 00:34:31,160
review the deal before you sign anything.

1039
00:34:31,510 --> 00:34:33,205
Let's recap the fifteen.

1040
00:34:33,385 --> 00:34:34,383
Septic pumping.

1041
00:34:34,563 --> 00:34:35,573
Dumpster rental.

1042
00:34:35,753 --> 00:34:37,135
Grease trap cleaning.

1043
00:34:37,315 --> 00:34:38,685
Biohazard cleanup.

1044
00:34:38,865 --> 00:34:39,805
Pest control.

1045
00:34:39,985 --> 00:34:41,309
Portable toilets.

1046
00:34:41,489 --> 00:34:42,662
Junk removal.

1047
00:34:42,842 --> 00:34:43,991
Pressure washing.

1048
00:34:44,171 --> 00:34:45,460
Trash can cleaning.

1049
00:34:45,640 --> 00:34:46,719
Commercial cleaning.

1050
00:34:46,899 --> 00:34:48,351
Dead animal removal.

1051
00:34:48,531 --> 00:34:49,634
Self storage.

1052
00:34:49,814 --> 00:34:51,137
Mobile home parks.

1053
00:34:51,317 --> 00:34:52,420
Drain cleaning.

1054
00:34:52,600 --> 00:34:53,715
And scrap metal.

1055
00:34:54,065 --> 00:34:55,388
And the pattern behind them.

1056
00:34:55,568 --> 00:34:56,857
Required demand.

1057
00:34:57,037 --> 00:34:58,279
Recurring revenue.

1058
00:34:58,459 --> 00:34:59,446
Weak competition.

1059
00:34:59,626 --> 00:35:01,948
Reusable assets that stay busy.

1060
00:35:02,128 --> 00:35:04,166
Plus one psychological edge:

1061
00:35:04,166 --> 00:35:06,713
the work most people avoid is often

1062
00:35:06,713 --> 00:35:08,096
the work that pays.

1063
00:35:08,446 --> 00:35:09,549
One last thought.

1064
00:35:09,729 --> 00:35:12,349
Every town in America has people quietly

1065
00:35:12,349 --> 00:35:14,772
earning a great living from work that

1066
00:35:14,772 --> 00:35:15,754
nobody notices.

1067
00:35:15,934 --> 00:35:17,815
The septic truck on your street,

1068
00:35:17,815 --> 00:35:20,049
the crew cleaning offices at midnight,

1069
00:35:20,049 --> 00:35:22,107
the person who hauled away your old

1070
00:35:22,107 --> 00:35:22,459
couch.

1071
00:35:22,639 --> 00:35:24,490
Behind many of those trucks is an

1072
00:35:24,490 --> 00:35:26,789
owner who decided that the money mattered

1073
00:35:26,789 --> 00:35:27,910
more than the image.

1074
00:35:28,090 --> 00:35:30,333
That choice is available to anyone willing

1075
00:35:30,333 --> 00:35:30,921
to make it,

1076
00:35:30,921 --> 00:35:32,897
and the competition for it is smaller

1077
00:35:32,897 --> 00:35:33,698
than you think.

1078
00:35:34,048 --> 00:35:36,177
If one of these businesses made you

1079
00:35:36,177 --> 00:35:37,942
curious instead of disgusted,

1080
00:35:37,942 --> 00:35:40,375
that's a sign worth paying attention to.

1081
00:35:40,555 --> 00:35:42,857
Pick one, study your local market this

1082
00:35:42,857 --> 00:35:45,098
week, and talk to someone who already

1083
00:35:45,098 --> 00:35:45,582
does it.

1084
00:35:45,762 --> 00:35:46,912
I'm Ryan Rover.

1085
00:35:47,092 --> 00:35:48,962
Stay boring, stay profitable,

1086
00:35:48,962 --> 00:35:50,768
and I'll see you in the next

1087
00:35:50,768 --> 00:35:51,155
video.
